   "text": "I read the image as the peptide named under it, H-Cpa-cyclo[D-Cys-Tyr-D-Aph(Cit)-Lys-Thr-Cys]-D-Tyr-NH2, and wrote it residue by residue from the N-terminus.\n\n- **N-terminus:** 4-chlorophenylalanine (Cpa) with a free amine, attached to the first Cys.\n- **Ring:** D-Cys, Tyr, D-Aph(Cit), Lys, Thr and Cys are linked in that order. The two Cys side chains are joined by a disulfide bond (ring closure label 2 in the SMILES).\n- **Aph(Cit):** a 4-aminophenylalanine whose ring nitrogen is acylated by citrulline. The citrulline keeps a free \u03b1-amine and a terminal ureido group, NHC(=O)NH2.\n- **C-terminus:** D-Tyr as a primary amide, attached to the last Cys.\n\nI did not read the wedges and hashes atom by atom. I took the stereochemistry from the residue names: L for Cpa, Tyr, Lys, Thr, Cys and Cit, and D for the first Cys, Aph and the C-terminal Tyr. The Cit configuration in particular is an assumption.\n\nSMILES: N[C@@H](Cc1ccc(Cl)cc1)C(=O)N[C@H](CS2)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc3ccc(O)cc3)C(=O)N[C@H](Cc3ccc(NC(=O)[C@@H](N)CCCNC(N)=O)cc3)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCN)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](CS2)C(=O)N[C@H](Cc3ccc(O)cc3)C(N)=O"
